<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Avalon Peninsula</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Avalon Peninsula is a large peninsula in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, joined to the rest of the island by a narrow isthmus. It contains St John's, the provincial capital, and was the earliest area of European fishing and settlement in Newfoundland, including Lord Baltimore's colony of Avalon at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferryland">Ferryland</a> from 1621 and the French base of Plaisance, now Placentia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/avalon-peninsula.jpg" alt="Avalon Peninsula" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Avalon_Peninsula.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
